  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Fine-tuning a black soldier flies processing technology</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">There are an estimated 1,200 active black soldier flies (BSF) larvae farmers active in Kenya. The largest part (more than 95%) are small and medium-sized (SME) farmers who lack capital and scale to invest in the expensive, imported, industrial dryers and could be supported with an alternative technology.The purpose of this project is to adapt existing semi-moist processing technology to the Kenyan context and testing its feasibility for mid-scale BSF farmers by setting up a pilot processing plant in Eldoret.Through this pilot Kenyan producers are able to see how the technology works and a production line is being built. It will also provide more insights on how these BSF producers will be able to actually benefit from it in terms of affordable equipment, knowledge on processing the larvae and a viable business model.</narrative>
  </description>
